{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc | sed -n '950,1360p'\"","aggregated_output":"   950\t\n   951\t(defn- exit-with!\n   952\t  \"Print a composition that ends at startup -- `--dht-keygen` -- and end\n   953\t   the process with its status.\"\n   954\t  [{:keys [lines exit]}]\n   955\t  (doseq [line lines]\n   956\t    (println line))\n   957\t  #?(:cljd (io/exit exit)\n   958\t     :clj (.halt (Runtime/getRuntime) (int exit))\n   959\t     :cljs (.exit js/process exit)))\n   960\t\n   961\t\n   962\t(defn- custody-control-step\n   963\t  \"The custody control plane's tick (r3 1.12): the renewals, pending\n   964\t   releases and request retries of every holder, the judge step and the\n   965\t   front steps of whatever custody composition the shell carries.  It\n   966\t   runs immediately after the DHT step and before the refusal and\n   967\t   admission branches, so custody progress and cleanup do not wait for\n   968\t   a hydration to finish and survive a refused store.  No program work\n   969\t   happens here whatever the shell's state.\"\n   970\t  [state]\n   971\t  (if-some [c (custody-of state)]\n   972\t    (assoc-in state [:repl :custody] (compose/control-step c))\n   973\t    state))\n   974\t\n   975\t\n   976\t(defn- custody-program-step\n   977\t  \"The custody program step's tick: activation, execution and export\n   978\t   preparation under the split driver's own revalidated tenure.  It runs\n   979\t   after the shell's own step and before the endpoint's, and never once\n   980\t   the shell has stopped -- the stop latch is set in the shell's place.\"\n   981\t  [state]\n   982\t  (if-some [c (custody-of state)]\n   983\t    (assoc-in state [:repl :custody] (compose/program-step c))\n   984\t    state))\n   985\t\n   986\t\n   987\t(defn- custody-stop\n   988\t  \"Latch the local stop on every holder of the shell's custody\n   989\t   composition (compose/stop): program work ends, control cleanup\n   990\t   continues through the bounded shutdown drain.  Idempotent, and a\n   991\t   no-op with no composition.\"\n   992\t  [state]\n   993\t  (if-some [c (custody-of state)]\n   994\t    (assoc-in state [:repl :custody] (compose/stop c))\n   995\t    state))\n   996\t\n   997\t\n   998\t(defn- custody-owed?\n   999\t  \"True while the shell's custody composition owes a control-plane\n  1000\t   write (compose/owed-control-write?): a pending write keeps the tick\n  1001\t   owner's cadence at the base interval, like the driver's own.\"\n  1002\t  [state]\n  1003\t  (if-some [c (custody-of state)]\n  1004\t    (compose/owed-control-write? c)\n  1005\t    false))\n  1006\t\n  1007\t\n  1008\t(defn step-all\n  1009\t  \"One tick of the single step owner: the local shell first, then the served\n  1010\t   endpoint, against the same shell value.  A DHT index store's node is stepped\n  1011\t   first (yin.repl.dht/step): its lines print before the shell's, a\n  1012\t   hydration still outstanding leaves every typed line waiting in the\n  1013\t   input medium, and a refused one stops the shell.  The custody control\n  1014\t   plane is stepped next, before the refusal and admission branches, so\n  1015\t   renewals, pending releases and request retries continue during\n  1016\t   hydration and past a refusal.  A `--port` process\n  1017\t   serves one shared shell, as v1's atom made it: the driver evaluates this\n  1018\t   tick's local\n  1019\t   lines first, so a definition typed at the local prompt is already in the\n  1020\t   shell the endpoint evaluates remote requests against in the same tick, and\n  1021\t   the endpoint's shell (remote definitions included) is threaded back\n  1022\t   before the next tick.  The custody program step follows the driver's own\n  1023\t   step and precedes the endpoint's; once the shell has stopped it is\n  1024\t   replaced by the stop latch, so no custody program call runs after\n  1025\t   `:running?` turns false.  A require parked on a closure load the node\n  1026\t   ended this tick is re-checked once, before any typed line, with no line\n  1027\t   of its own (yin.repl/recheck-on-tick, yin.vm.linker.dht.md 8.2),\n  1028\t   and linker progress resumes a parked run (7.5): its text prints after the\n  1029\t   node's lines.  Returns `[state server lines]`;\n  1030\t   the caller only prints.\"\n  1031\t  [state server now]\n  1032\t  (let [[repl dht-lines events] (repl.dht/step (:repl state) now)\n  1033\t        state (custody-control-step (assoc state :repl repl))]\n  1034\t    (cond\n  1035\t      (repl.dht/refusal repl)\n  1036\t      [(custody-stop (assoc state :running? false)) server dht-lines]\n  1037\t\n  1038\t      (not (repl.dht/admitting? repl))\n  1039\t      [state server dht-lines]\n  1040\t\n  1041\t      :else\n  1042\t      (let [[repl rechecked] (shell/recheck-on-tick (:repl state) events)\n  1043\t            dht-lines (cond-> dht-lines\n  1044\t                        (seq rechecked) (conj rechecked))\n  1045\t            state (assoc state :repl repl)\n  1046\t            stepped (driver/repl-step state now)\n  1047\t            stepped (if (:running? stepped)\n  1048\t                      (custody-program-step stepped)\n  1049\t                      (custody-stop stepped))\n  1050\t            [entries state'] (driver/take-outbox stepped)\n  1051\t            server' (when server\n  1052\t                      (serve/step (assoc-in server [:repl] (:repl state'))\n  1053\t                                  now))\n  1054\t            [server-entries server''] (if server'\n  1055\t                                        (serve/take-outbox server')\n  1056\t                                        [[] nil])\n  1057\t            state'' (if server'' (assoc state' :repl (:repl server'')) state')]\n  1058\t        [state'' server'' (into dht-lines\n  1059\t                                (map entry-text)\n  1060\t                                (into (vec entries) server-entries))]))))\n  1061\t\n  1062\t\n  1063\t(defn moved?\n  1064\t  \"The tick owner's cadence bit, computed from this tick's own results: true\n  1065\t   when there are lines to print, when the endpoint reports movement (a\n  1066\t   woken probe, a published notice), or when either composition still owes a\n  1067\t   write -- the shell's own or a custody control-plane one.  A pending write\n  1068\t   keeps cadence at the base interval; it must never wait out a backoff\n  1069\t   ceiling.\"\n  1070\t  [state server lines]\n  1071\t  (boolean (or (seq lines)\n  1072\t               (driver/pending-write? state)\n  1073\t               (repl.dht/busy? (:repl state))\n  1074\t               (custody-owed? state)\n  1075\t               (and server (serve/moved? server)))))\n  1076\t\n  1077\t\n  1078\t(defn exit-status\n  1079\t  \"The process status a host exits with once the shell stops: 1 when the\n  1080\t   DHT store refused after startup (a failed bind, a hydration that could\n  1081\t   not complete), else 0.\"\n  1082\t  [state]\n  1083\t  (if (repl.dht/refusal (:repl state)) 1 0))\n  1084\t\n  1085\t\n  1086\t;; =============================================================================\n  1087\t;; Shutdown\n  1088\t;; =============================================================================\n  1089\t\n  1090\t(def stop-ticks\n  1091\t  \"How many ticks a host steps a stopping endpoint before exiting anyway.  The\n  1092\t   endpoint's `:stopped` fact comes from the host's own close completion, which\n  1093\t   a wedged listener may never deposit; the shell says so and exits rather than\n  1094\t   hanging on it.\"\n  1095\t  200)\n  1096\t\n  1097\t\n  1098\t(def stop-timeout-text\n  1099\t  \";; the endpoint did not report :stopped; exiting anyway\")\n  1100\t\n  1101\t\n  1102\t(def stop-join-millis\n  1103\t  \"How long a host thread may wait for the step owner to finish shutdown.\n  1104\t\n  1105\t   The drain performs `stop-ticks + 1` steps with a sleep between them, so it\n  1106\t   needs strictly more than `tick-millis x stop-ticks`; a join of exactly that\n  1107\t   expires mid-drain and the announced timeout never prints.\"\n  1108\t  (* tick-millis (+ stop-ticks 2)))\n  1109\t\n  1110\t\n  1111\t(defn request-stop!\n  1112\t  \"The explicit stop trigger: append the shell's own quit line to the input\n  1113\t   medium.\n  1114\t\n  1115\t   This is the whole of what a host signal handler, a headless supervisor, or a\n  1116\t   test does to stop the composition.  It is a line producer like any other, so\n  1117\t   the one step owner still performs the shutdown: `(quit)` stops the shell,\n  1118\t   and the shell stopping is what stops the endpoint.  The wake source, when\n  1119\t   one is supplied, is nudged so the step owner runs the quit line at once\n  1120\t   rather than at the idle interval it had armed.\"\n  1121\t  ([state]\n  1122\t   (driver/submit-line! (:input state) \"(quit)\"))\n  1123\t  ([state w]\n  1124\t   (let [result (request-stop! state)]\n  1125\t     (when w (wake/nudge! w))\n  1126\t     result)))\n  1127\t\n  1128\t\n  1129\t(defn stop-tick\n  1130\t  \"One shutdown tick for the shell's head board and the endpoint, both of\n  1131\t   which have already been asked to stop (`yin.repl.dht/stop!`,\n  1132\t   `serve/stop!`).  Returns `[state server lines stopped?]`, the node's\n  1133\t   lines before the endpoint's.\n  1134\t\n  1135\t   `serve/stopped?` is the whole of the endpoint's exit condition, and\n  1136\t   `yin.repl.dht/stopped?` for the shell's head board: an endpoint that never\n  1137\t   bound is done on the first tick, because no host exists to report a\n  1138\t   `:stopped` fact for it, an absent endpoint -- a shell run without\n  1139\t   `--port` -- never had one, and so is a shell with no board.  The custody\n  1140\t   composition is not stepped here: `shutdown-tick` is the drain tick that\n  1141\t   wraps this one with the custody control plane.\"\n  1142\t  [state server now]\n  1143\t  (let [[repl dht-lines _] (repl.dht/step (:repl state) now)\n  1144\t        state (assoc state :repl repl)\n  1145\t        [server' entries] (if server\n  1146\t                            (let [[entries server'] (serve/take-outbox\n  1147\t                                                      (serve/step server now))]\n  1148\t                              [server' entries])\n  1149\t                            [nil []])]\n  1150\t    [state server'\n  1151\t     (into (vec dht-lines) (map entry-text) entries)\n  1152\t     (and (or (nil? server') (serve/stopped? server'))\n  1153\t          (repl.dht/stopped? repl))]))\n  1154\t\n  1155\t\n  1156\t(defn shutdown-enter?\n  1157\t  \"Whether a shell that just stopped enters the bounded shutdown drain at\n  1158\t   all (r3 1.12 as amended by residual 4 and the D15 gate's shutdown row):\n  1159\t   there is an endpoint to stop, a head board that still owes its\n  1160\t   stop-and-drain, or a custody composition that still owes a\n  1161\t   control-plane write.  A REPL run without --port enters the drain on its\n  1162\t   owed custody writes alone -- a release owed at quit is sent, never\n  1163\t   dropped by the process exit.\"\n  1164\t  [state server]\n  1165\t  (boolean (or server\n  1166\t               (get-in state [:repl :dht])\n  1167\t               (custody-owed? state))))\n  1168\t\n  1169\t\n  1170\t(defn shutdown-drained?\n  1171\t  \"The bounded shutdown drain's exit condition, the one every host loop\n  1172\t   tests: the endpoint has stopped -- an absent endpoint owes nothing --\n  1173\t   AND the shell's head board owes nothing at exit, AND the custody\n  1174\t   composition owes no further control-plane write.  A pending release,\n  1175\t   renewal or undelivered reply still owed keeps the drain stepping\n  1176\t   within its `stop-ticks` budget; the budget, not this predicate, is\n  1177\t   what bounds a write that can never complete.\"\n  1178\t  [state server]\n  1179\t  (boolean (and (serve/stopped? server)\n  1180\t                (repl.dht/stopped? (:repl state))\n  1181\t                (not (custody-owed? state)))))\n  1182\t\n  1183\t\n  1184\t(defn shutdown-tick\n  1185\t  \"One tick of the bounded shutdown drain (r3 1.12, residual 4), the tick\n  1186\t   every host's drain loop calls: the custody control plane keeps running --\n  1187\t   the holders' local stop latch is set here, at drain entry, on every host,\n  1188\t   including paths that reached the drain without another normal `step-all`\n  1189\t   -- and the head board and the endpoint drain (an absent endpoint drains\n  1190\t   nothing and answers stopped).  No custody program step runs: program\n  1191\t   execution stays stopped once the shell has.  Returns\n  1192\t   `[state server lines stopped?]`; the budget (`stop-ticks`) and the exit\n  1193\t   condition (`shutdown-enter?`, `shutdown-drained?`) are the caller's.\"\n  1194\t  [state server now]\n  1195\t  (let [state (custody-control-step (custody-stop state))]\n  1196\t    (stop-tick state server now)))\n  1197\t\n  1198\t\n  1199\t;; =============================================================================\n  1200\t;; clj: a reader thread that only appends, and one owned poller thread\n  1201\t;; =============================================================================\n  1202\t\n  1203\t#?(:cljd\n  1204\t   nil\n  1205\t   :clj\n  1206\t   (do\n  1207\t     (defn- print-prompt!\n  1208\t       []\n  1209\t       (print prompt)\n  1210\t       (flush))\n  1211\t\n  1212\t     (defn- drain!\n  1213\t       \"The shell has quit, so the head board, the endpoint and the custody\n  1214\t        control plane stop before the host exits: ask the board and the\n  1215\t        endpoint once, then keep stepping all three until the endpoint has\n  1216\t        stopped AND the board owes nothing AND custody owes no further\n  1217\t        control write (`shutdown-drained?`), or the bounded budget runs\n  1218\t        out.  The drain is entered at all only when one of them owes\n  1219\t        something (`shutdown-enter?` -- a shell with no endpoint enters it\n  1220\t        on owed custody writes alone).  A connected client must observe the\n  1221\t        ended answer, not the bare close a process exit would leave behind.\n  1222\t        The bounded drain sleeps the base interval; it is a budget, not a\n  1223\t        cadence.  The custody control plane steps on every one of its ticks\n  1224\t        (`shutdown-tick`); the state it reaches is durable in the progress\n  1225\t        journal, so what the budget leaves outstanding is a restart's to\n  1226\t        resend.  Answers the drained state.\"\n  1227\t       [state server w]\n  1228\t       (if (shutdown-enter? state server)\n  1229\t         (loop [state (update state :repl repl.dht/stop!)\n  1230\t                server (some-> server serve/stop!)\n  1231\t                remaining stop-ticks]\n  1232\t           (let [[state' server' lines _stopped?]\n  1233\t                 (shutdown-tick state server (System/currentTimeMillis))]\n  1234\t             (doseq [line lines]\n  1235\t               (println line))\n  1236\t             (cond\n  1237\t               (shutdown-drained? state' server') state'\n  1238\t               (zero? remaining) (do (println stop-timeout-text) state')\n  1239\t               :else (do (wake/sleep! w tick-millis)\n  1240\t                         (recur state' server' (dec remaining))))))\n  1241\t         state))\n  1242\t\n  1243\t     (defn poll-loop!\n  1244\t       \"The sole owner of REPL and endpoint state on the JVM.  It carries both\n  1245\t        values through serial steps; nothing is shared with the reader.\n  1246\t\n  1247\t        Its cadence is `cadence/cadence-step` over `default-cadence`, slept\n  1248\t        through the wake source `w` (one is made when the caller supplied\n  1249\t        none): any line the reader deposits, and the explicit stop trigger,\n  1250\t        nudges it, so operator actions never wait out the idle curve.\n  1251\t\n  1252\t        It also owns the exit.  The reader is parked in `read-line` and cannot\n  1253\t        observe that the shell has quit, so a typed `(quit)` would otherwise\n  1254\t        stop the endpoint and then wait for end-of-input that only Ctrl-D\n  1255\t        produces.  `exit!` is called once, by this thread, after the endpoint\n  1256\t        has drained.\"\n  1257\t       ([state server headless?]\n  1258\t        (poll-loop! state server headless? #(.halt (Runtime/getRuntime) 0)))\n  1259\t       ([state server headless? exit!]\n  1260\t        (poll-loop! state server headless? exit! (wake/make-wake)))\n  1261\t       ([state server headless? exit! w]\n  1262\t        (loop [state state\n  1263\t               server server\n  1264\t               cadence (cadence/init default-cadence)]\n  1265\t          (let [[state' server' lines] (step-all state server\n  1266\t                                                 (System/currentTimeMillis))]\n  1267\t            (doseq [line lines]\n  1268\t              (println line))\n  1269\t            (if (:running? state')\n  1270\t              (do (when (and (seq lines) (not headless?))\n  1271\t                    (print-prompt!))\n  1272\t                  (let [{:keys [cadence-state sleep-ms]}\n  1273\t                        (cadence/cadence-step cadence\n  1274\t                                              (moved? state' server' lines))]\n  1275\t                    (wake/sleep! w sleep-ms)\n  1276\t                    (recur state' server' cadence-state)))\n  1277\t              (let [state' (drain! state' server' w)]\n  1278\t                (println)\n  1279\t                (close-index-store! state')\n  1280\t                (let [status (exit-status state')]\n  1281\t                  (if (zero? status)\n  1282\t                    (exit!)\n  1283\t                    (.halt (Runtime/getRuntime) (int status))))))))))\n  1284\t\n  1285\t     (defn- read-loop!\n  1286\t       \"The reader parks in `read-line` and appends, nudging the step owner's\n  1287\t        wake: a typed line ends the idle sleep at once.  It reads no state.\"\n  1288\t       [input w]\n  1289\t       (loop []\n  1290\t         (if-let [line (read-line)]\n  1291\t           (do (driver/submit-line! input line)\n  1292\t               (wake/nudge! w)\n  1293\t               (recur))\n  1294\t           (do (driver/submit-line! input \"(quit)\")\n  1295\t               (wake/nudge! w)))))\n  1296\t\n  1297\t     (defn -main\n  1298\t       [& args]\n  1299\t       (let\n  1300\t         [started (startup args {:persist? true})]\n  1301\t         (when (contains? started :exit) (exit-with! started))\n  1302\t         (if-some\n  1303\t           [refusal (:refusal started)]\n  1304\t           (refuse! refusal)\n  1305\t           (let\n  1306\t             [{:keys [opts state server]} started\n  1307\t              headless? (boolean (:headless? opts))\n  1308\t              w (wake/make-wake)]\n  1309\t             (doseq [line (banner opts)]\n  1310\t               (println line))\n  1311\t             (let\n  1312\t               [poller (Thread.\n  1313\t                         ^Runnable (fn []\n  1314\t                                     (poll-loop!\n  1315\t                                       state\n  1316\t                                       server\n  1317\t                                       headless?\n  1318\t                                       #(.halt\n  1319\t                                          (Runtime/getRuntime) 0)\n  1320\t                                       w)))]\n  1321\t               (.setDaemon poller true)\n  1322\t               (.start poller)\n  1323\t               ;; Headless attends the endpoint only: there is no reader, so the\n  1324\t               ;; step owner is joined until it stops, and the explicit stop\n  1325\t               ;; trigger\n  1326\t               ;; is the host signal a shutdown hook observes.  The hook appends\n  1327\t               ;; a\n  1328\t               ;; line like any producer, nudges, and then waits for the one\n  1329\t               ;; step\n  1330\t               ;; owner.\n  1331\t               (if headless?\n  1332\t                 (do (.addShutdownHook\n  1333\t                       (Runtime/getRuntime)\n  1334\t                       (Thread. ^Runnable (fn []\n  1335\t                                            (request-stop! state w)\n  1336\t                                            (.join poller ^long\n  1337\t                                                   stop-join-millis))))\n  1338\t                     (.join poller))\n  1339\t                 (do (print-prompt!)\n  1340\t                     ;; End-of-input is one way to stop; a typed `(quit)` is the\n  1341\t                     ;; other, and the step owner has already exited the process\n  1342\t                     ;; by\n  1343\t                     ;; the time this join is reached in that case.\n  1344\t                     ;; The join is unbounded: lines read before end-of-input\n  1345\t                     ;; still evaluate ahead of its `(quit)`, and the step\n  1346\t                     ;; owner bounds its own shutdown drain (`stop-ticks`)\n  1347\t                     ;; and exits the process itself.\n  1348\t                     (read-loop! (:input state) w)\n  1349\t                     (.join poller))))\n  1350\t             (.halt (Runtime/getRuntime) 0)))))))\n  1351\t\n  1352\t\n  1353\t;; =============================================================================\n  1354\t;; cljs (Node): a readline handler that only appends, and one interval owner\n  1355\t;; =============================================================================\n  1356\t\n  1357\t#?(:cljs\n  1358\t   (do\n  1359\t     (defn run-node!\n  1360\t       \"The tick owner on Node: one wake source arms exactly one timer per\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
