{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"git diff HEAD -- test/yin/repl/dht_process_test.clj; nl -ba test/yin/repl/dht_process_test.clj | sed -n '1,210p'; tail -100 test/yin/repl/dht_process_test.clj; cat deps.edn\"","aggregated_output":"git: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-E0oXCsPP' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n2026-10-17 18:01:34.080 xcodebuild[99119:70569991]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\n2026-10-17 18:01:34.363 xcodebuild[99119:70569986] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \"Input/output error\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-KRAjlzui' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n2026-10-17 18:01:35.050 xcodebuild[99127:70570021]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\n2026-10-17 18:01:35.330 xcodebuild[99127:70570020] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \"Input/output error\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\ndiff --git a/test/yin/repl/dht_process_test.clj b/test/yin/repl/dht_process_test.clj\nindex c2bc3014b..2a95c26c3 100644\n--- a/test/yin/repl/dht_process_test.clj\n+++ b/test/yin/repl/dht_process_test.clj\n@@ -1180,3 +1180,53 @@\n           ((:stop! anchor))\n           (io/delete-file key-file true)\n           (run! delete-dir! dirs))))))\n+\n+\n+(defn- run-submissions\n+  \"Type `submissions` into the spawned REPL `s`, close stdin, and wait up\n+   to `ms` for exit. Returns {:exited bool, :lines [output lines],\n+   :exit-code}. The child's stdout is block-buffered on a pipe, so output\n+   lines appear in bulk at exit; under the regression the process never\n+   exits and is destroyed at the deadline.\"\n+  [s submissions ms]\n+  (doseq [line submissions] (type! s line))\n+  (.close ^java.io.Writer (:stdin s))\n+  (let [process ^java.lang.Process (:process s)\n+        done   (.waitFor process ms java.util.concurrent.TimeUnit/MILLISECONDS)]\n+    (when-not done (.destroy process))\n+    {:exited done\n+     :lines @(:lines s)\n+     :exit-code (when done (.exitValue process))}))\n+\n+\n+(deftest ^:slow prompt-returns-after-filtered-comprehension-assignment-test\n+  \"Regression for the owner's live-session hang: at the JVM prompt, after\n+   `(lang :yang.python/antlr)`, a filtered comprehension assignment\n+   never came back. With stdin closed after the lines, `-main` halted\n+   the process `stop-join-millis` after end-of-input, while the lines\n+   were still evaluating, so nothing they printed ever appeared.\n+\n+   Both sessions must evaluate every line before their end-of-input\n+   `(quit)` and exit: the control (a lang switch plus a trivial print)\n+   and the owner's filtered comprehension, read back by a print.\"\n+  (let [control (run-submissions\n+                  (spawn! \"prompt-hang-control\"\n+                          [\"--name\" \"prompt-hang-control\"\n+                           \"--dir\" \"target/prompt-hang-control\"])\n+                  [\"(lang :yang.python/antlr)\" \"print(1+2)\"] 90000)\n+        bug     (run-submissions\n+                  (spawn! \"prompt-hang-bug\"\n+                          [\"--name\" \"prompt-hang-bug\"\n+                           \"--dir\" \"target/prompt-hang-bug\"])\n+                  [\"(lang :yang.python/antlr)\"\n+                   \"even_squares = [x**2 for x in range(1, 11) if x % 2 == 0]\"\n+                   \"print(even_squares)\"]\n+                  90000)]\n+    (is (:exited control) \"the control session exited promptly\")\n+    (is (some #(re-find #\"Switched to\" %) (:lines control))\n+        \"the control lang switch was processed\")\n+    (is (:exited bug)\n+        \"THE BUG: the comprehension session never exited; it hung on the\n+         filtered comprehension submission\")\n+    (is (some #(re-find #\"\\[4, 16, 36, 64, 100\\]\" %) (:lines bug))\n+        \"the comprehension session stored and printed the even squares\")))\n     1\t(ns yin.repl.dht-process-test\n     2\t  \"DHT epic S5 across real processes and real loopback sockets\n     3\t   (docs/design/dao.jing.dht.md section 10): separate `yin.repl.main`\n     4\t   JVMs, each over its own locked `dht:<dir>`, exchange content through\n     5\t   their UDP sockets.\n     6\t\n     7\t   Two fetch-only listeners and one publisher: the publisher's round\n     8\t   prints its result at once and its publication is later reported\n     9\t   acknowledged, sent to 2 peers.  Then a reader handed the manifest\n    10\t   address the publisher printed hydrates the publisher's index over the\n    11\t   network before it evaluates the lines already typed at it, and its `q`\n    12\t   answers the publisher's facts under the publisher's session token.\n    13\t\n    14\t   No port is reserved ahead of time.  The first node is an anchor in\n    15\t   this JVM (a `dao.jing.dht` core node over the JVM datagram seam,\n    16\t   bound to port 0), and every REPL process binds an ephemeral port and\n    17\t   reports it (`listening on host:port`); each later process is handed\n    18\t   the addresses already reported.\n    19\t\n    20\t   Each directory is locked by its owner: a plain `dao.space.dht/join`\n    21\t   and a second REPL process on the publisher's directory are both\n    22\t   refused, naming it.  The Node reader is required: build it with\n    23\t   `bb build:yin-repl-node`; a missing build fails this test.\n    24\t\n    25\t   Linker over DHT slice L5 (docs/design/yin.vm.linker.dht.md section 12)\n    26\t   is the end-to-end gate: a JVM publisher holding a key file publishes a\n    27\t   module by name; JVM and Node readers handed its index manifest and\n    28\t   principal require it by name and evaluate the export on each of the\n    29\t   four VMs; a reader that does not declare the principal is refused; and\n    30\t   plain Clojure in this JVM takes the same path through the functions\n    31\t   the REPL's host functions call, failure results included.  Its\n    32\t   in-process form, over the mesh seam on all three hosts, is\n    33\t   yin.vm.linker.dht-end-to-end-test.\n    34\t\n    35\t   Real processes wait on sockets, so this test polls their output with\n    36\t   bounded deadlines; the DHT core itself still sees only ticks.\"\n    37\t  (:require [clojure.java.io :as io]\n    38\t            [clojure.string :as str]\n    39\t            [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n    40\t            [dao.datom :as datom]\n    41\t            [dao.jing :as jing]\n    42\t            [dao.jing.dht :as jing.dht]\n    43\t            [dao.jing.mem :as mem]\n    44\t            [dao.space.dht :as dht]\n    45\t            [dao.space.dht-test :as dht-test]\n    46\t            [dao.stream :as stream]\n    47\t            [dao.stream.datagram :as datagram]\n    48\t            [dao.stream.datagram.jvm :as datagram.jvm]\n    49\t            [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ringbuffer]\n    50\t            [yin.repl.main :as main]\n    51\t            [yin.vm :as vm]\n    52\t            [yin.vm.ast-walker :as ast-walker]\n    53\t            [yin.vm.debruijn.register :as rvm]\n    54\t            [yin.vm.debruijn.stack :as dvm]\n    55\t            [yin.vm.linker :as linker]\n    56\t            [yin.vm.linker.closure-test :as ct]\n    57\t            [yin.vm.linker.dht :as ld]\n    58\t            [yin.vm.linker.publish :as publish]\n    59\t            [yin.vm.linker.sign :as sign]\n    60\t            [yin.vm.semantic :as semantic]\n    61\t            [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu])\n    62\t  (:import (java.util.concurrent TimeUnit)))\n    63\t\n    64\t\n    65\t(def ^:private startup-ms\n    66\t  \"Bound on one JVM REPL's startup: it loads the whole shell from source.\"\n    67\t  240000)\n    68\t\n    69\t\n    70\t(def ^:private exchange-ms\n    71\t  \"Bound on one network outcome once every process is up.\"\n    72\t  60000)\n    73\t\n    74\t\n    75\t(defn- ring\n    76\t  []\n    77\t  (:dao.stream/handle\n    78\t    (ringbuffer/create! {:dao.stream/type ringbuffer/transport-type\n    79\t                         ringbuffer/capacity-key 4096})))\n    80\t\n    81\t\n    82\t(def ^:private bind-ms\n    83\t  \"Bound on the anchor's socket reporting its bind.\"\n    84\t  10000)\n    85\t\n    86\t\n    87\t(defn- await-bound\n    88\t  \"The anchor socket's `:bound` event from `traffic`, polled until\n    89\t   `bind-ms` pass, or `{:failure text}`: a `:bind-failed` event, or no\n    90\t   lifecycle event in time.  On failure the seam is closed.\"\n    91\t  [seam traffic]\n    92\t  (let [deadline (+ (System/currentTimeMillis) bind-ms)\n    93\t        fail (fn [text]\n    94\t               ((:close! seam))\n    95\t               {:failure (str \"the anchor socket did not bind: \" text)})]\n    96\t    (loop [cursor (:dao.stream/cursor (stream/cursor traffic\n    97\t                                                     :dao.stream/oldest))]\n    98\t      (let [r (stream/next traffic cursor)\n    99\t            v (:dao.stream/value r)]\n   100\t        (cond\n   101\t          (not= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r))\n   102\t          (if (< (System/currentTimeMillis) deadline)\n   103\t            (do (Thread/sleep 5) (recur cursor))\n   104\t            (fail (str \"no bound event within \" bind-ms \" ms\")))\n   105\t\n   106\t          (= :dao.stream.datagram/bound (:dao.stream.datagram/event v))\n   107\t          {:bound v}\n   108\t\n   109\t          (= :dao.stream.datagram/bind-failed (:dao.stream.datagram/event v))\n   110\t          (fail (str \"bind-failed: \" (:dao.stream.datagram/reason v)))\n   111\t\n   112\t          :else (recur (:dao.stream/cursor r)))))))\n   113\t\n   114\t\n   115\t(defn- start-bound-anchor!\n   116\t  [seam traffic bound opts]\n   117\t  (let [port (get-in bound [:dao.stream.datagram/local\n   118\t                            :dao.stream.datagram/port])\n   119\t        ticks (ring)\n   120\t        state (jing.dht/state\n   121\t                (merge\n   122\t                  {:local (mem/create-content-mem)\n   123\t                   :requests (ring) :answers (ring) :facts (ring) :ticks ticks\n   124\t                   :traffic traffic\n   125\t                   :datagrams (datagram/writer\n   126\t                                seam\n   127\t                                {:dao.stream/type datagram/transport-type\n   128\t                                 :dao.stream/identity \"anchor\"\n   129\t                                 :dao.stream.datagram/bind-host \"127.0.0.1\"\n   130\t                                 :dao.stream.datagram/bind-port port}\n   131\t                                1200)\n   132\t                   ::jing.dht/id (jing.dht/bytes->hex (dht/secure-random-bytes\n   133\t                                                        32))\n   134\t                   ::jing.dht/secret (dht/secure-random-bytes 32)\n   135\t                   ::jing.dht/max-inbound-bytes 0}\n   136\t                  opts))\n   137\t        running (atom true)\n   138\t        origin (System/nanoTime)\n   139\t        thread (doto (Thread.\n   140\t                       ^Runnable\n   141\t                       (fn []\n   142\t                         (loop [state state]\n   143\t                           (when @running\n   144\t                             (stream/append! ticks\n   145\t                                             {:dao.lease/event :dao.lease/tick\n   146\t                                              :dao.lease/reading\n   147\t                                              (quot (- (System/nanoTime) origin)\n   148\t                                                    1000000)})\n   149\t                             (let [state (jing.dht/step state 64)]\n   150\t                               (Thread/sleep 5)\n   151\t                               (recur state)))))\n   152\t                       \"dht-process-anchor\")\n   153\t                 (.setDaemon true)\n   154\t                 (.start))]\n   155\t    {:port port\n   156\t     :stop! (fn []\n   157\t              (reset! running false)\n   158\t              (.join thread 1000)\n   159\t              ((:close! seam)))}))\n   160\t\n   161\t\n   162\t(defn- start-anchor!\n   163\t  \"The first node: a `dao.jing.dht` core node on an ephemeral loopback\n   164\t   port, which needs no bootstrap contact to hold a socket, stepped by\n   165\t   one owner thread with its monotonic clock as ticks.  Answers `{:port p\n   166\t   :stop! f}`, or `{:failure text}` when its socket did not bind (the\n   167\t   seam already closed).  `opts` merge into the core state: a storing\n   168\t   peer is `{::jing.dht/publish? true ::jing.dht/max-inbound-bytes n}`.\"\n   169\t  ([] (start-anchor! {}))\n   170\t  ([opts]\n   171\t   (let [traffic (ring)\n   172\t         seam (datagram.jvm/bind! {:identity \"anchor\" :deposit traffic\n   173\t                                   :bind-host \"127.0.0.1\" :bind-port 0\n   174\t                                   :max-bytes 1200})\n   175\t         {:keys [bound failure]} (await-bound seam traffic)]\n   176\t     (if failure\n   177\t       {:failure failure}\n   178\t       (start-bound-anchor! seam traffic bound opts)))))\n   179\t\n   180\t\n   181\t(def ^:private listening\n   182\t  #\"dht: node [0-9a-f]+ listening on 127\\.0\\.0\\.1:(\\d+)\")\n   183\t\n   184\t\n   185\t(defn- temp-dir\n   186\t  []\n   187\t  (str \"target/test-dht-process-\" (random-uuid)))\n   188\t\n   189\t\n   190\t(defn- delete-dir!\n   191\t  [dir]\n   192\t  (let [f (io/file dir)]\n   193\t    (when (.isDirectory f)\n   194\t      (doseq [child (.listFiles f)] (.delete child))\n   195\t      (.delete f))))\n   196\t\n   197\t\n   198\t(defn- jvm-command\n   199\t  \"`yin.repl.main` on a JVM over this test's classpath.\"\n   200\t  []\n   201\t  [(str (System/getProperty \"java.home\") \"/bin/java\")\n   202\t   \"-cp\" (System/getProperty \"java.class.path\")\n   203\t   \"clojure.main\" \"-m\" \"yin.repl.main\"])\n   204\t\n   205\t\n   206\t(def ^:private node-script\n   207\t  \"The Node build of `yin.repl.main` (shadow-cljs build `:yin-repl`),\n   208\t   built by `bb build:yin-repl-node`.\"\n   209\t  \"target/yin-repl.js\")\n   210\t\n                        (swap! procs conj p)\n                        p))\n               b (join \"reader-b-jvm\" (jvm-command) (dirs 1))\n               e (when (.exists (io/file node-script))\n                   (join \"reader-b-node\" [\"node\" node-script] (dirs 2)))\n               readers (remove nil? [b e])\n               _ (doseq [p readers] (first-contact-leg p))\n               ;; A comes back on the same port: its recovered HEAD is its\n               ;; board's first trace (5.4)\n               a (spawn! \"publisher-a-again\" (into a-args [\"--dht-port\"\n                                                           (str pa)]))]\n              (swap! procs conj a)\n              (testing \"A restarted on its port prints the same token\"\n                (is (= token (some->> (await-line a token-line startup-ms)\n                                      (re-find token-line)\n                                      second))\n                    (transcript a)))\n              (doseq [p readers] (follower-leg p principal))\n              (testing \"join saved --dht-follow\"\n                (is (str/includes? (slurp (str (dirs 1) \"/state.edn\"))\n                                   (str \":dht-follow [\\\"\" public \"@127.0.0.1:\"\n                                        pa \"\\\"]\"))))\n              (type! a \"(def f (fn [x] (+ x 4300)))\")\n              (type! a \"(require (quote yin.link))\")\n              (type! a \"(yin.link/publish (quote my.lib) (quote [f]))\")\n              (doseq [p readers] (moved-leg p))\n              (testing \"a reader restarted with A stopped still requires it\"\n                (stop! a)\n                (doseq [p readers] (stop! p))\n                (doseq [[label command dir] [[\"reader-b-jvm-again\" (jvm-command)\n                                              (dirs 1)]\n                                             (when e\n                                               [\"reader-b-node-again\"\n                                                [\"node\" node-script] (dirs 2)])]\n                        :when label]\n                  (let [p (spawn-stateful! label command [\"--dir\" dir])]\n                    (swap! procs conj p)\n                    (is (await-line p #\"dht: following ed25519:\\S+ at .*; installed head\"\n                                    startup-ms)\n                        (transcript p))\n                    (is (await-next p \"(require (quote my.lib))\"\n                                    #\"^(yin> )*'my\\.lib$\")\n                        (transcript p))\n                    (is (await-next p \"(my.lib/f 1)\" #\"^(yin> )*4301$\")\n                        (transcript p))))))))\n        (finally\n          (doseq [p @procs] (stop! p))\n          ((:stop! anchor))\n          (io/delete-file key-file true)\n          (run! delete-dir! dirs))))))\n\n\n(defn- run-submissions\n  \"Type `submissions` into the spawned REPL `s`, close stdin, and wait up\n   to `ms` for exit. Returns {:exited bool, :lines [output lines],\n   :exit-code}. The child's stdout is block-buffered on a pipe, so output\n   lines appear in bulk at exit; under the regression the process never\n   exits and is destroyed at the deadline.\"\n  [s submissions ms]\n  (doseq [line submissions] (type! s line))\n  (.close ^java.io.Writer (:stdin s))\n  (let [process ^java.lang.Process (:process s)\n        done   (.waitFor process ms java.util.concurrent.TimeUnit/MILLISECONDS)]\n    (when-not done (.destroy process))\n    {:exited done\n     :lines @(:lines s)\n     :exit-code (when done (.exitValue process))}))\n\n\n(deftest ^:slow prompt-returns-after-filtered-comprehension-assignment-test\n  \"Regression for the owner's live-session hang: at the JVM prompt, after\n   `(lang :yang.python/antlr)`, a filtered comprehension assignment\n   never came back. With stdin closed after the lines, `-main` halted\n   the process `stop-join-millis` after end-of-input, while the lines\n   were still evaluating, so nothing they printed ever appeared.\n\n   Both sessions must evaluate every line before their end-of-input\n   `(quit)` and exit: the control (a lang switch plus a trivial print)\n   and the owner's filtered comprehension, read back by a print.\"\n  (let [control (run-submissions\n                  (spawn! \"prompt-hang-control\"\n                          [\"--name\" \"prompt-hang-control\"\n                           \"--dir\" \"target/prompt-hang-control\"])\n                  [\"(lang :yang.python/antlr)\" \"print(1+2)\"] 90000)\n        bug     (run-submissions\n                  (spawn! \"prompt-hang-bug\"\n                          [\"--name\" \"prompt-hang-bug\"\n                           \"--dir\" \"target/prompt-hang-bug\"])\n                  [\"(lang :yang.python/antlr)\"\n                   \"even_squares = [x**2 for x in range(1, 11) if x % 2 == 0]\"\n                   \"print(even_squares)\"]\n                  90000)]\n    (is (:exited control) \"the control session exited promptly\")\n    (is (some #(re-find #\"Switched to\" %) (:lines control))\n        \"the control lang switch was processed\")\n    (is (:exited bug)\n        \"THE BUG: the comprehension session never exited; it hung on the\n         filtered comprehension submission\")\n    (is (some #(re-find #\"\\[4, 16, 36, 64, 100\\]\" %) (:lines bug))\n        \"the comprehension session stored and printed the even squares\")))\n{:deps {org.clojure/core.async {:mvn/version \"1.8.741\"}\n        org.clojure/tools.reader {:mvn/version \"1.5.0\"}\n        ring/ring {:mvn/version \"1.14.1\"}\n        com.cognitect/transit-clj {:mvn/version \"1.0.333\"}\n        org.replikativ/boring {:mvn/version \"0.1.30\"}\n        com.datomic/peer {:mvn/version \"1.0.7364\"}\n        org.postgresql/postgresql {:mvn/version \"42.7.3\"}\n        org.clojure/data.json {:mvn/version \"2.5.0\"}\n        http-kit/http-kit {:mvn/version \"2.8.0\"}\n        org.jsoup/jsoup {:mvn/version \"1.18.3\"}\n        instaparse/instaparse {:mvn/version \"1.5.0\"}\n        ;; yang.python.antlr: the runtime the generated Python3 parser runs\n        ;; on; pinned to the tool version in :antlr-gen (they are one release)\n        org.antlr/antlr4-runtime {:mvn/version \"4.13.2\"}\n        criterium/criterium {:mvn/version \"0.4.6\"}\n        io.github.rctcwyvrn/blake3 {:mvn/version \"1.3\"}\n        stigmergy/chp {:mvn/version \"0.1.0-SNAPSHOT\"\n                       :exclusions [refactor-nrepl/refactor-nrepl]}}\n :cljd/opts {}\n ;; build/antlr/python3/classes: the generated Python3 parser, produced by\n ;; `clj -M:antlr-gen` (antlr/python3/manifest.edn); absent until generated\n :paths [\"src/clj\" \"src/cljc\" \"src/cljs\" \"src/cljd\"\n         \"build/antlr/python3/classes\"]\n :aliases {:clean {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n                   :exec-fn clean/clean}\n           :profile-btree {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n                           :extra-deps {persistent-sorted-set/persistent-sorted-set\n                                        {:mvn/version \"0.3.0\"}}\n                           :main-opts [\"-m\" \"btree-bench\"]}\n           :test {:extra-paths [\"test\"]\n                  :extra-deps {io.github.cognitect-labs/test-runner\n                               {:git/tag \"v0.5.1\" :git/s